# Build context for `Dockerfile`. Everything the image needs is listed in the
# Dockerfile's COPY lines: the Rust workspace, `sidecar/livesync-sidecar`, and the
# packaged data directories (skills, obsidian-snippets, assets). Nothing else has
# any business travelling to the daemon.
#
# `target/` is the expensive one: a local `cargo build` leaves gigabytes there, and
# shipping it would both slow every build and invalidate the layer cache on each
# host-side rebuild. The image builds Rust in its own stage, from sources, so the
# host's artifacts are not merely unnecessary — they must not be reachable.
target/
**/node_modules/
sidecar/livesync-sidecar/dist/

.git/
.github/
.claude/
outputs/
**/.DS_Store
**/.deep-obsidian-mcp/

# Docs and other packaging channels the image does not use. `*.md` has no `**/`
# prefix on purpose: it drops the root-level documents (README, CHANGELOG, ...) and
# leaves `skills/**/SKILL.md` — which the image does install — untouched.
*.md
docs/
Formula/
packaging/
